body:
I ran into the same on 4.5dev5, it seems to be a performance issue that gets progressively worse the smaller the `texture_region_size` value is.

With a `texture_region_size` of `(2, 2)` the editor doesn't freeze completely, but still becomes unbearably slow. When the tileset tab is closed the slowdown goes away. Increasing the region size progressively reduces the slowdown.

Zooming in or out does not affect performance.

This is the code I'm using for testing, in case anyone with more engine know-how feels like trouble-shooting:
```
		# Create tileset source.
		var source : TileSetAtlasSource = TileSetAtlasSource.new();
		source.texture = load("res://atlas.png");
		source.texture_region_size = Vector2i.ONE * 4;

		# Create tileset.
		var tileset : TileSet = TileSet.new();
		tileset.tile_size = Vector2i.ONE * 64;
		tileset.add_source(source);

		# Save.
		ResourceSaver.save(tileset, "res://tileset.tres");
		EditorInterface.get_resource_filesystem().scan();
```
